  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Standard Operating Procedures of Externally-Financed projects</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activities to be carried out under this grant are:  Component 1 - Develop Standard Operating Procedures (SOP).  Technical assistance would be provided to MOFA to help prepare harmonized SOP that would provide detailed guidance on how to identify, prepare, appraise, implement, monitor and evaluate projects and programs financed by development partners. The SOP would clarify roles, responsibilities, accountabilities of all concerned agencies, and streamline procedures. Component 2 - Develop a Financial Management Manual (FMM).  Technical assistance would be provided to MOF to prepare a harmonized FMM for development projects and programs that would provide detailed guidance and procedures on all areas of financial management including policies and procedures, planning and budgeting, funds flow and cash management, accounting systems and practices, reporting and audit monitoring and arrangement. Component 3 - Dissemination and capacity development. This component would consist of training and workshops. The recently produced SOP and FMM in Cambodia under an IDF Grant will be used as a reference, always adapting it to the Lao-PDR context.</narrative>
  </description>
